    [Doc][Misc] Correct GLM deployment examples and parameter guidance (#19581)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Correct confirmed inconsistencies in the GLM-5/5.1 and GLM-5.3-Flash
    tutorials: match the query request to its chat response, align the
    second 950DT Decode stage and the summary with the existing 135000-token
    limit, clarify MTP token budgets and the independent roles of eager
    execution and chunked prefill, and describe layout-dependent concurrency
    limits. Express the Flash A3 hardware consistently as 16 logical devices
    with 64GB each. Update its PD and KV pool examples to Decode DP4/TP4 and
    three MTP tokens on both roles, enable shared-expert DP on Decode, and
    synchronize launcher, proxy and pool lookup-port descriptions. Keep
    recorded accuracy results labeled with their original tested topology.
    Unify Flash reasoning parsers to glm47 throughout the serving examples,
    FAQ and bilingual parameter description. Align the GLM-5.3 950DT
    ordinary PD example with the supplied PP2/TP8 Prefill and DP16/TP1
    Decode reference, enable Prefill shared-expert multistream overlap and
    update the matching launch commands and proxy endpoints. Its KV pooling
    and 1M scenarios are unchanged.
    
    The 950DT ordinary 2P1D example now explicitly starts two independent
    PP2/TP8 Prefill instances on P0/P1 and P2/P3 (four Prefill nodes). Each
    PP group uses its own master, and the proxy registers only P0 and P2.
    The shared DP16/TP1 Decode group remains on D0/D1. KV pooling and 1M
    configurations are unchanged. Compared this structure with Kimi-K2.6
    2P1D and the existing GLM A2 two-instance PP2 pooling scripts.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation examples and their Chinese translations are corrected. The
    GLM-5.2/5.3 and GLM-5.3-Flash Prefill-Decode examples explicitly set
    engine_id, including ordinary PD, KV cache pooling and 1M context PD.
    GLM-5/5.1 examples retain automatic IDs. The Flash A3 PD and GLM-5.3
    950DT ordinary PD Decode layouts change as described above; unrelated
    platform scripts and startup settings are preserved. Superseded examples
    from the reported issue list are not reintroduced.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - English and Chinese MkDocs strict builds.
    - Markdownlint, codespell, typos and git diff --check.
    - Checked request JSON, all four 950DT stage limits and summary rows,
    and the limited executable-example diff.
    - Verified translated code blocks, inline parameters, table/heading
    structure and local anchors; no new untranslated prose relative to the
    base.
    - Verified all 34 PD configurations for GLM-5.2/5.3 and Flash (including
    KV cache pooling and 1M context) include engine_id, IDs restart at zero
    and are distinct within each independent deployment scenario, Chinese
    code examples match, and this follow-up changes only engine_id fields.
    - Checked the Flash A3 configuration JSON, Bash syntax, four Decode
    endpoints, lookup-port ranges and Chinese descriptions; executable
    examples outside the A3 PD tab remain unchanged in this update.
    - Checked the 950DT ordinary PD configuration JSON, Bash syntax, all 16
    DP rank/device mappings and proxy endpoints; the shared launcher source,
    KV pooling and 1M scenarios are unchanged.
    - No NPU inference run; the hardware edit clarifies logical-device
    notation rather than changing the topology.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c0b6f74bee518aeaf5d72b200a0216e72fbb5e7c
    
